WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.445
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:12.050
Stanford lies at the
heart of Silicon Valley.

00:00:12.050 --> 00:00:14.150
And when you think
of Silicon Valley

00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:16.930
and by implication
Stanford, you think

00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:20.550
of the people who take
risks, break boundaries.

00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:22.740
That's the reason why I
think Stanford, indeed,

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:25.195
is a unique place to
understand innovation

00:00:25.195 --> 00:00:26.680
and entrepreneurship.

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:28.800
We have cherry
picked, to be honest,

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:31.030
the best Stanford
faculty we can find

00:00:31.030 --> 00:00:32.860
in entrepreneurship
and innovation.

00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:34.406
On one hand you'll
have people who

00:00:34.406 --> 00:00:35.780
will do a more
rigorous research,

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:37.300
like my colleague,
Hayagreeva Rao.

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:41.000
On the other hand, you'll have
folks like Perry Klebahn, who

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:43.460
actually invented
the modern snowshoe.

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:46.020
So we have that sort of range
of folks, to bring together,

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:48.420
if you will, the rigorous
and the relevant.

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:52.280
What the certificate program and
the courses in the certificate

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:58.860
program do is they inform people
about cutting edge practices.

00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:03.380
They illuminate
principles underlying

00:01:03.380 --> 00:01:05.319
innovation and entrepreneurship.

00:01:05.319 --> 00:01:09.050
But most of all,
they inspire people.

00:01:09.050 --> 00:01:10.700
So that you can go
out and innovate

00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:12.940
and be an entrepreneur
in your own company

00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:14.560
or in your own
corner of the world.

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:16.950
Taught by world renowned
faculty from the Graduate

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:19.410
School of Business and
the School of Engineering,

00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:22.400
the Stanford Innovation and
Entrepreneurship certificate

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:26.010
is a self-paced
interactive online program,

00:01:26.010 --> 00:01:30.000
where you will gain essential
skills and effective strategies

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.180
to generate and
implement new ideas.

00:01:32.180 --> 00:01:34.170
There are many
features that Stanford

00:01:34.170 --> 00:01:37.090
can offer to make the
Innovation and Entrepreneurship

00:01:37.090 --> 00:01:40.070
certificate suit the needs
of your organization.

00:01:40.070 --> 00:01:42.810
Your company's private
branded landing page

00:01:42.810 --> 00:01:45.060
is the hub of your program.

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:46.850
From the landing
page, participants

00:01:46.850 --> 00:01:50.730
can enter the discussion forum,
preview upcoming webinars,

00:01:50.730 --> 00:01:52.990
join the virtual
study hall, connect

00:01:52.990 --> 00:01:56.080
with other participants,
read about the faculty,

00:01:56.080 --> 00:01:58.190
and access their courses.

00:01:58.190 --> 00:02:00.550
Each course is
divided into modules

00:02:00.550 --> 00:02:03.320
and contains lectures,
interactive assignments,

00:02:03.320 --> 00:02:05.090
and readings.

00:02:05.090 --> 00:02:07.440
Throughout the course,
the Stanford teaching team

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:11.440
will provide participants with
feedback on select assignments,

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:13.390
challenging them to
apply their knowledge

00:02:13.390 --> 00:02:15.900
and hone their
innovation skills.

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:18.250
There are a number of
courses to choose from,

00:02:18.250 --> 00:02:20.740
so you can customize
the program to fit

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:22.065
the needs of your organization.

00:02:22.065 --> 00:02:24.940
So one of our design
principles in the classes

00:02:24.940 --> 00:02:27.675
is anywhere you have
good internet access,

00:02:27.675 --> 00:02:28.550
you can take a class.

00:02:28.550 --> 00:02:30.780
So your employees
throughout your company

00:02:30.780 --> 00:02:33.030
get to be exposed to
them in a way where

00:02:33.030 --> 00:02:35.890
they have control over
their time and can pace it.

00:02:35.890 --> 00:02:38.860
What companies can do is
signal to their high potential

00:02:38.860 --> 00:02:41.000
individuals, hey,
you're valuable.

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:42.920
We need you, we want you.

00:02:42.920 --> 00:02:44.770
One of the things
about innovation

00:02:44.770 --> 00:02:46.600
is if you want to do
better, you better

00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:49.120
spread it throughout
the organization.

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:51.452
If you're working even
in a large company,

00:02:51.452 --> 00:02:53.660
and you want to make sure
that your large company has

00:02:53.660 --> 00:02:55.880
the soul of a startup,
this program's

00:02:55.880 --> 00:02:58.450
a great place to begin with.

